.TH ITCMDR\-SERVER 1 "" "itcmdr" "itcmdr manual"
.SH NAME
itcmdr\-server \- the site server (gRPC for the agents, HTTPS API for the apps)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
itcmdr\-server [\-\-console | \-\-service]
itcmdr\-server init
itcmdr\-server recover\-db\-key
itcmdr\-server hash\-token TOKEN
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the site server. With no argument or \fB--console\fR it runs in the foreground; \fB--service\fR runs as the Windows service. \fBinit\fR and \fBrecover-db-key\fR are the same as in \fBitcmdr-cli\fR(1). \fBhash-token\fR prints the stored hash of a legacy shared token. Settings come from server.json (see \fBITCMDR_SERVER_CONFIG\fR) and the database; see the settings guide.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ITCMDR_SERVER_CONFIG
path of server.json
.TP
.B ITCMDR_DATA_DIR
data folder (\-\-data\-dir beats it; it beats server.json)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_SERVER_PROGRAM
the server program folder for self\-upgrade (default: the exe's folder)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_RESTORE_BIN
path of itcmdr\-restore (default: next to the server)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_PLUGIN_PS_HOST
path of itcmdr\-plugin\-ps (default: next to the exe)
.TP
.B ITCMDR_POWERSHELL
PowerShell to run (default powershell.exe on Windows, pwsh elsewhere)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBitcmdr\fR(7), docs/README.md (also the in-app help: \fBitcmdr-cli help\fR, \fBitcmdr-admin help\fR)
